  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "One contract, three clients",
      "items": [
        "The console, the employee portal and the Android app all consume the same generated API client over /api/v1.",
        "Router registration: backend/app/api/v1/router.py:40-47. The demo router is added only when demo mode is on."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Authentication is pluggable; authorization is enforced server-side",
      "items": [
        "auth_provider defaults to `demo` (an X-Demo-Actor-Id header) for local work; `supabase` is the production provider, verifying a token against the project JWKS with an explicit issuer, audience and algorithm allow-list.",
        "The client is never trusted to state who it is: permission checks and organization scoping happen in the service layer."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "What is deliberately not claimed here",
      "items": [
        "Extraction is drawn with a dashed edge: EXTRACTION_PROVIDER defaults to `unavailable` and the other providers fail closed, so no text is proven to be extracted.",
        "The policy pre-flight is advisory and writes nothing - verified: zero session.add / session.commit calls.",
        "No payment or reimbursement execution exists anywhere in this codebase."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Data stores",
      "items": [
        "PostgreSQL holds 28 application tables across four migrations.",
        "audit_events is append-only via the trg_audit_events_append_only trigger (migration 0001:1837-1855). That is database integrity, not cryptographic immutability and not WORM storage.",
        "Receipt bytes are private objects, served only through an authorization-checked endpoint, never a public URL."
      ]
    }
  ]
